{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "f0e1d2c3-4b5a-6978-8a9b-0c1d2e3f4a5b",
    "name": "Fortezy POS Client Backend",
    "description": "HTTP API for the Fortezy POS (Point of Sale) client backend.\n\n## Getting started\n1. Start the server: `go run .` (defaults to http://localhost:8080).\n2. Adjust the `baseUrl` collection variable if needed.\n3. Run **Auth > Login** first. It stores the returned JWT in the `token`\n   collection variable, which every protected request uses via Bearer auth.\n4. Store-scoped requests (categories, products, sales) additionally require the\n   logged-in user to be assigned to a store, otherwise they return `403`.\n\n## Suggested run order\nLogin (saves `token`) → Users > Get current user → Categories > List →\nProducts > List (saves `productId`) → Products > Get detail (saves `variantId`)\n→ Sales > Create (saves `saleId`) → Sales > List → Sales > Get detail →\nSales > Void.\n\nList/detail requests write IDs into collection variables so later requests can\nreference them ({{productId}}, {{saleId}}, ...).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
